WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.451 --> 00:00:11.347
Tom Lindqvist: Hey Michelle, hey Brandon. How's it going over there?

2
00:00:11.831 --> 00:00:20.565
Michelle Tran: Hey Tom. Busy week. We just finished open enrollment for the sales floor, so half my team is out, but we're getting through it.

3
00:00:21.735 --> 00:00:27.579
Brandon Hughes: Yeah, and Q3 closed out yesterday, so everybody's buried in reporting. But good to see you.

4
00:00:27.903 --> 00:00:42.636
Tom Lindqvist: Nice. I won't keep you long. I mostly wanted to check in on call volumes and see how the PreSense side is holding up, since we talked about it a couple times this quarter.

5
00:00:43.861 --> 00:00:51.174
Brandon Hughes: Volumes are up. August was around 41,000 inbound across the sales queues, and September looks like it'll land close to 44,000.

6
00:00:51.174 --> 00:00:53.960
Brandon Hughes: The fiber promo drove a lot of that.

7
00:00:54.802 --> 00:00:59.686
Tom Lindqvist: That's a solid jump. How's the routing holding up with that volume?

8
00:01:01.041 --> 00:01:10.982
Brandon Hughes: Mostly fine. The sales queues are where we feel it. We had to add two more agents to the Denver queue last week to keep wait times reasonable.

9
00:01:12.009 --> 00:01:18.999
Michelle Tran: Which is partly why I want to bring something up. It's the transfer thing again, and it's gotten worse.

10
00:01:20.132 --> 00:01:21.889
Tom Lindqvist: Okay, tell me more.

11
00:01:22.245 --> 00:01:30.975
Michelle Tran: So when a call gets transferred from one queue to another, or from one agent to another, the receiving agent's screen pop comes up empty.

12
00:01:30.975 --> 00:01:35.165
Michelle Tran: No journey, no page history, nothing. Just a blank panel in Genesys.

13
00:01:36.395 --> 00:01:39.859
Tom Lindqvist: Is that on every transfer, or specific types?

14
00:01:40.921 --> 00:01:49.497
Michelle Tran: It's the warm ones. If the agent does a cold transfer with the original call leg intact, the pop shows up fine.

15
00:01:49.497 --> 00:01:58.853
Michelle Tran: But when they do a warm transfer, where the first agent stays on and introduces, the pop is blank for whoever picks it up.

16
00:01:59.615 --> 00:02:02.908
Tom Lindqvist: And when did you first start noticing this?

17
00:02:04.405 --> 00:02:13.953
Michelle Tran: We saw it maybe six weeks ago, but it was intermittent. Now it's pretty much every warm transfer in the sales queues.

18
00:02:13.953 --> 00:02:18.727
Michelle Tran: My leads are complaining because agents go into the call blind.

19
00:02:20.091 --> 00:02:31.320
Brandon Hughes: It's not just annoying. We're seeing handle time go up by maybe forty seconds on those calls because the second agent has to ask everything again.

20
00:02:32.244 --> 00:02:40.646
Tom Lindqvist: Okay. Do you have a recent example, a call ID or timestamp, that I can hand to the team?

21
00:02:41.346 --> 00:02:50.877
Michelle Tran: I can pull a few. There was one yesterday, maybe 2:15 PM, transferred from the Denver sales queue to the retention queue.

22
00:02:50.877 --> 00:02:54.342
Michelle Tran: I'll send you the interaction ID this afternoon.

23
00:02:55.743 --> 00:03:04.115
Tom Lindqvist: Perfect. And is this affecting the Genesys side only, or are you seeing anything odd in the Invoca reporting?

24
00:03:05.606 --> 00:03:15.696
Michelle Tran: Just Genesys. The Invoca side looks normal. Signals are firing, the call logs are complete, it's only the screen pop that goes blank.

25
00:03:16.495 --> 00:03:26.937
Tom Lindqvist: Got it. I'll take that back to the team and see what they need. In the meantime, is there a workaround your leads can use?

26
00:03:27.523 --> 00:03:35.084
Michelle Tran: Right now they're just telling agents to cold transfer if they can. But that's not always the right call for the customer.

27
00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:40.878
Tom Lindqvist: Understood. I'll flag it and follow up by Friday with an update.

28
00:03:42.046 --> 00:03:52.024
Brandon Hughes: Appreciate it. On the flip side, the Google Ads offline conversions are still flowing fine, and Adobe Analytics is picking up the call data like it should.

29
00:03:52.024 --> 00:03:53.133
Brandon Hughes: No issues there.

30
00:03:53.504 --> 00:03:58.533
Tom Lindqvist: Good to hear. How's the AI Voice Agent handling the after hours traffic?

31
00:03:59.541 --> 00:04:08.068
Brandon Hughes: It's doing its job. Overnight calls are mostly billing questions and it routes them to the right place. Nothing to report.

32
00:04:08.597 --> 00:04:11.574
Tom Lindqvist: Great. Anything else on your radar before we wrap?

33
00:04:12.925 --> 00:04:15.921
Michelle Tran: Not from me. I'll get you those call examples.

34
00:04:17.036 --> 00:04:18.727
Brandon Hughes: Same here. Thanks Tom.

35
00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:24.674
Tom Lindqvist: Sounds good. I'll send a follow-up note and we'll talk soon.
